IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- wra-core.l4: the shared nouns of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (United Kingdom), 2012 c. 5.
-- DECLARE only: no rule, no #EVAL. The four part agents (wra1 to wra4) import this file read-only.
-- Source: inputs/ukpga-2012-5.txt, a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from legislation.gov.uk
-- (version 2026-07-01). It is not the official text, and nothing here is verified against the official text.
-- A line `-- src:N | text` copies line N of that file.
--
-- Conventions for every module that imports this one:
--   * money is a NUMBER of pounds sterling, and a rate is per week unless its name says otherwise;
--   * dates are `Date day month year` (from daydate), and a span of days is a Period;
--   * a record holds facts a witness could state; whether the Act's test is met is a rule, in a part;
--   * when the Act leaves a value to regulations, the rule takes it as a MAYBE input and answers NOTHING on NOTHING (PLAN.md);
--   * a name that is in this file may not be defined again; a name a part needs and lacks goes in its NEEDS-CORE.md.

§ `Where a person is`

-- src:32 | (c) is in Great Britain,
-- src:1536 | (a) £25,323 or £16,967, for persons resident in Greater London;
@ref s 4(1)(c) (src:32), s 96(5A)(a) (src:1536)
DECLARE Place IS ONE OF
    `Greater London`                   -- England, within Greater London (the only part of England the Act singles out)
    `England outside Greater London`
    Scotland
    Wales
    `Northern Ireland`
    `outside the United Kingdom`

§ `People`

-- src:30 | (a) is at least 18 years old,
-- src:31 | (b) has not reached the qualifying age for state pension credit,
-- src:32 | (c) is in Great Britain,
@ref s 4(1)(a)-(c) (src:30-32)
DECLARE Person HAS
    `reference`              IS A STRING     -- tells one person from another; equality of this field is identity
    `age in years`           IS A NUMBER     -- completed years on the day the question is about
    `date of birth`          IS A DATE       -- for a rule that runs on some other day than the question's
    `where the person is`    IS A Place      -- presence ("is in Great Britain", s 4(1)(c))
    `where the person lives` IS A Place      -- residence ("persons resident in Greater London", s 96(5A)(a))

-- The three facts s 39(1) turns on, as a witness would state them. They do not say whether the two people ARE a couple.
-- src:422 | (a) two people who are married to, or civil partners of, each other and are members of the same household; or
-- src:423 | (b) two people who are not married to, or civil partners of, each other but are living together as if they were a married couple or civil partners.
@ref s 39(1)(a)-(b) (src:422-423)
DECLARE `Relationship of two people` HAS
    `married to each other or civil partners of each other` IS A BOOLEAN
    `members of the same household`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `living together as if married or civil partners`       IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Two people` HAS
    `the first person`  IS A Person
    `the second person` IS A Person
    `their relationship` IS A `Relationship of two people`

-- How the claim is made, not what the people are: a member of a couple may claim as a single person (s 2(2)).
-- src:7 | (2) Universal credit may, subject as follows, be awarded to—
-- src:8 | (a) an individual who is not a member of a couple (a “single person”), or
-- src:9 | (b) members of a couple jointly.
@ref s 1(2) (src:7-9)
DECLARE Claimants IS ONE OF
    `a single claimant` HAS `the single claimant` IS A Person
    `joint claimants`   HAS `the joint claimants` IS A `Two people`

-- The claimants and the children and young persons in their household. Whether a claimant is "responsible" for one is left to regulations.
DECLARE Household HAS
    `the claimants`                 IS A Claimants
    `the children and young persons` IS A LIST OF Person

-- src:1711 | (b) requiring the employer, on being served with a notice by the Secretary of State, to make deductions from the earnings of the beneficiary and to pay corresponding amounts to the Secretary of State;
@ref s 105 inserting 71ZD(3)(b) (src:1711)
DECLARE Employer HAS
    `the employer's reference` IS A STRING

§ `Who decides, who is owed, who is subject to a power`

-- The decision-makers and other holders of a power or a duty that the Act names, other than the individual. Never a seat.
-- src:350 | (1) The functions of the Secretary of State under sections 13 to 25 may be exercised by, or by the employees of, such person as the Secretary of State may authorise for the purpose (an “authorised person”).
-- src:587 | (c) without a good reason refuses or fails to apply for, or accept if offered, a situation in any employment which an employment officer has informed him is vacant or about to become vacant;
-- src:1342 | “the Commissioners” means the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs;
-- src:1661 | (1) Schedule 12 contains amendments reinstating powers to make decisions superseding decisions made by appellate bodies before their functions were transferred to the First-tier Tribunal and Upper Tribunal.
-- src:1724 | (1) Where an amount is recoverable under section 71ZB from a person residing in England and Wales, the amount is, if the county court so orders, recoverable—
-- src:2289 | (a) the Director of Public Prosecutions;
@ref s 29(1) (src:350), s 46 inserting JSA 19(2)(c) (src:587), s 76(3) (src:1342), s 103(1) (src:1661), s 105 inserting 71ZE(1) (src:1724), s 128 (src:2289)
DECLARE Authority IS ONE OF
    `the Secretary of State`
    `an authorised person`                -- s 29(1): a person the Secretary of State authorises (contracting out)
    `an employment officer`               -- JSA 19(2)(c)
    `Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs`   -- "the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs"
    `a local authority`
    `the First-tier Tribunal`
    `the Upper Tribunal`
    `a court`                             -- the county court (England and Wales) or the sheriff court (Scotland), 71ZE
    `the Director of Public Prosecutions`

§ `Benefits, awards and payments`

-- Every benefit the Act names as one that is paid or abolished, one constructor each. "Jobseeker's allowance" and
-- "employment and support allowance" without a qualifier cover both of their constructors.
-- src:382 | (1) The following benefits are abolished—
-- src:383 | (a) income-based jobseeker's allowance under the Jobseekers Act 1995;
-- src:1556 | “welfare benefit” means—
-- src:1570 | widowed parent's allowance (see section 39A of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992).
@ref s 33(1)-(2) (src:382-383), s 96(10) (src:1556-1570)
DECLARE Benefit IS ONE OF
    `universal credit`
    `contribution-based jobseeker's allowance`
    `income-based jobseeker's allowance`                -- s 33(2)(a): the meaning it has in the Jobseekers Act 1995
    `contributory employment and support allowance`
    `income-related employment and support allowance`   -- s 33(2)(b): entitlement based on s 1(2)(b) of the Welfare Reform Act 2007
    `income support`
    `housing benefit`
    `council tax benefit`
    `child tax credit`
    `working tax credit`
    `state pension credit`
    `housing credit`                                    -- the housing element of state pension credit (Schedule 4)
    `personal independence payment`
    `disability living allowance`
    `industrial injuries benefit`
    `social fund payment`                               -- a discretionary payment (ss 70-73)
    `child benefit`
    `guardian's allowance`
    `bereavement allowance`
    `incapacity benefit`
    `maternity allowance`
    `severe disablement allowance`
    `widow's pension`
    `widowed mother's allowance`
    `widowed parent's allowance`

-- Both days count. Used for an assessment period, a reference period, a period of entitlement, a period a payment was for.
DECLARE Period HAS
    `first day` IS A DATE
    `last day`  IS A DATE

DECLARE Award HAS
    `the benefit awarded`       IS A Benefit
    `who it is awarded to`      IS A Claimants
    `the period awarded for`    IS A Period
    `the amount awarded for the period, in pounds` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Kind of payment` IS ONE OF
    `a payment of an award`
    `a payment on account`    -- s 101
    `a hardship payment`      -- s 28; JSA 19C; ESA 16A

DECLARE Payment HAS
    `the kind of payment`        IS A `Kind of payment`
    `the benefit paid`           IS A Benefit
    `the person it was paid to`  IS A Person
    `the period paid for`        IS A Period
    `the amount paid for the period, in pounds` IS A NUMBER

§ `Work-related requirements and sanctions`

-- src:131 | (2) In this Part “work-related requirement” means—
-- src:132 | (a) a work-focused interview requirement (see section 15);
-- src:133 | (b) a work preparation requirement (see section 16);
-- src:134 | (c) a work search requirement (see section 17);
-- src:135 | (d) a work availability requirement (see section 18).
@ref s 13(2) (src:131-135)
DECLARE `Work-related requirement` IS ONE OF
    `work-focused interview requirement`   -- s 15
    `work preparation requirement`         -- s 16
    `work search requirement`              -- s 17
    `work availability requirement`        -- s 18

-- src:136 | (3) The work-related requirements which may be imposed on a claimant depend on which of the following groups the claimant falls into—
-- src:137 | (a) no work-related requirements (see section 19);
-- src:138 | (b) work-focused interview requirement only (see section 20);
-- src:139 | (c) work-focused interview and work preparation requirements only (see section 21);
-- src:140 | (d) all work-related requirements (see section 22).
@ref s 13(3) (src:136-140)
DECLARE `Group of claimants by requirement` IS ONE OF
    `no work-related requirements`                                 -- s 19
    `work-focused interview requirement only`                      -- s 20
    `work-focused interview and work preparation requirements only` -- s 21
    `all work-related requirements`                                -- s 22

-- Each way the Act (or an Act it inserts into) reduces an award for a failure. Named together in Schedule 5 para 1(3)
-- and Schedule 6 para 5(4), so the parts that hold those and the parts that hold the sections must share the list.
-- src:3060 | (a) section 26 or 27,
-- src:3061 | (b) section 6J or 6K of the Jobseekers Act 1995, or
-- src:3062 | (c) section 11J of the Welfare Reform Act 2007.
-- src:3164 | section 26 or 27 above,
-- src:3165 | section 19, 19A or 19B of the Jobseekers Act 1995,
-- src:3166 | section 11, 12 or 13 of the Welfare Reform Act 2007, or
-- src:3167 | section 2A, 2AA or 2D of the Social Security Administration Act 1992.
@ref Sch 5 para 1(3) (src:3060-3062), Sch 6 para 5(4) (src:3164-3167)
DECLARE `Provision that reduces an award` IS ONE OF
    `universal credit higher-level sanction`                       -- s 26
    `universal credit other sanction`                              -- s 27
    `jobseeker's allowance higher-level sanction`                  -- JSA 19, inserted by s 46
    `jobseeker's allowance other sanction`                         -- JSA 19A, inserted by s 46
    `jobseeker's allowance ceasing to be available`                -- JSA 19B, inserted by s 46
    `jobseeker's allowance higher-level sanction after universal credit` -- JSA 6J, inserted by s 49
    `jobseeker's allowance other sanction after universal credit`  -- JSA 6K, inserted by s 49
    `employment and support allowance interim sanction`            -- WRA2007 ss 11-13, named in Sch 6 para 5(4)
    `employment and support allowance sanction`                    -- WRA2007 11J, inserted by s 57
    `income support sanction`                                      -- SSAA 2A, 2AA, 2D, named in Sch 6 para 5(4)

§ `Personal independence payment`

-- src:1348 | (2) A person's entitlement to personal independence payment may be an entitlement to—
-- src:1349 | (a) the daily living component (see section 78);
-- src:1350 | (b) the mobility component (see section 79); or
-- src:1351 | (c) both those components.
@ref s 77(2) (src:1348-1351)
DECLARE `Component of personal independence payment` IS ONE OF
    `daily living component`   -- s 78
    `mobility component`       -- s 79

-- src:1355 | (1) A person is entitled to the daily living component at the standard rate if—
-- src:1358 | (2) A person is entitled to the daily living component at the enhanced rate if—
@ref s 78(1)-(2) (src:1355-1358)
DECLARE `Rate of a component` IS ONE OF
    `standard rate`
    `enhanced rate`

DECLARE `Entitlement to a component` HAS
    `the component` IS A `Component of personal independence payment`
    `the rate`      IS A `Rate of a component`

§ `Decisions, challenging them, and recovering an amount`

-- Decisions the Act itself names. Which of them carries a right of appeal is a rule (s 97(6), s 105), not a fact.
-- src:407 | (3) The question whether a claimant has limited capability for work or work-related activity for the purposes of this Part is to be determined in accordance with regulations.
-- src:1388 | (1) For the purposes of this Part, the following questions are to be determined in accordance with regulations—
-- src:1598 | A decision to apply the benefit cap in accordance with regulations under section 96 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012.
-- src:1780 | A decision as to the amount of payment recoverable under section 71ZB, 71ZG or 71ZH of the Administration Act.
-- src:2855 | A decision as to the amount of a relevant benefit that is payable to a person by virtue of regulations under section 6B, 7, 8 or 9 of the Social Security Fraud Act 2001.
@ref s 37(3) (src:407), s 80(1) (src:1388), s 97(6) inserting SSA1998 Sch 2 para 8A (src:1598), s 105(7) inserting SSA1998 Sch 3 para 6B (src:1780), Sch 2 adding to SSA1998 Sch 3 after para 3 (src:2855)
DECLARE `Kind of decision` IS ONE OF
    `a decision on entitlement to a benefit or on its amount`
    `a decision on limited capability for work or work-related activity`  -- s 37(3)
    `a decision on ability to carry out daily living or mobility activities` -- s 80(1)
    `a decision to apply the benefit cap`                                 -- s 96; s 97(6)
    `a decision that an amount is recoverable or on how much`             -- 71ZB, 71ZG, 71ZH
    `a decision on the amount payable after loss of benefit for an offence` -- SSFA 6B, 7, 8, 9

DECLARE Decision HAS
    `the kind of decision` IS A `Kind of decision`
    `the decision-maker`   IS A Authority
    `the benefit concerned` IS A Benefit
    `the date it was made` IS A DATE

-- src:1633 | (2) In section 12 (appeals to First-tier Tribunal), in subsection (2)—
-- src:1638 | (3A) Regulations may provide that, in such cases or circumstances as may be prescribed, there is a right of appeal under subsection (2) in relation to a decision only if the Secretary of State has considered whether to revise the decision under section 9.
-- src:1687 | (a) reversed or varied on an appeal, or
-- src:1688 | (b) revised or superseded under section 9 or section 10 of the Social Security Act 1998,
@ref s 102(2) (src:1633), s 102(3) inserting SSA1998 12(3A) (src:1638), s 105 inserting 71ZB(3) (src:1687-1688)
DECLARE `Step after a decision` IS ONE OF
    `revision`                                             -- SSA 1998 s 9
    `supersession`                                         -- SSA 1998 s 10
    `consideration of revision before an appeal`           -- SSA 1998 12(3A), where regulations require it
    `appeal to the First-tier Tribunal`                    -- SSA 1998 s 12
    `appeal to the Upper Tribunal`

-- src:1693 | (7) An amount recoverable under this section may (without prejudice to any other means of recovery) be recovered—
-- src:1694 | (a) by deduction from benefit (section 71ZC);
-- src:1695 | (b) by deduction from earnings (section 71ZD);
-- src:1696 | (c) through the courts etc (section 71ZE);
-- src:1697 | (d) by adjustment of benefit (section 71ZF).
@ref s 105 inserting 71ZB(7) (src:1693-1697)
DECLARE `Way of recovering an amount` IS ONE OF
    `deduction from benefit`      -- 71ZC
    `deduction from earnings`     -- 71ZD
    `court action`                -- 71ZE
    `adjustment of benefit`       -- 71ZF
